title The work that stood on no ref
prompt Take the Diffuser baton, close reds first, carry the moonshot lane forward.
think Round-open named four parked paths in the dead-letter box and on no ref, and the claim board carried a live diffuser claim over exactly those paths -- so the lane's next move was already built and unlanded rather than unstarted.
think The 175931 account had named this loom one lap earlier and prescribed the cure: land the record FIRST rather than recover a sixth time. Recovering and then building again would have been the seventh firing.
think Restored the five untracked files from the stash's third parent, applied the two clean tracked hunks, and re-seated the shelf row by hand because two newer rows had landed above its old insertion point.
think Placed the row by STAMP rather than at the top: 182429 is older than 182600, and the shelf reads newest first, so prepending blindly would have put the day out of order.
think Re-ran the witness on metal rather than trusting a recovered GREEN, then chased a reading that looked wrong -- names=254 where the paper says 510 -- until it resolved as the witness's own deliberate --names 256 bound rather than a silent population loss.
obs THE WITNESS IS GREEN ON METAL AT 43 OF 43 LEGS, four mutations bitten, both verdicts reachable from planted populations.
obs THE PAPER'S FIGURES REPRODUCE at the default population: chi_prefix 13149.11 against its 13134.05, roomdist_prefix 0.395 against 0.410, recovery 0.5333 against 0.5353, plurality 0.3471 exactly. The drift is tree growth over one day, and both clauses declare every figure FREE, which is what makes the drift readable rather than a lie.
obs THE CARD ACCOUNT CARRIES THIS LAP'S READING rather than the stashed lap's, since figures already an hour stale on the day they land teach a reader to stop checking.
obs AIR FELT A BOUNDARY IN THE FINDING ITSELF. Single-stranded gives the paper's central claim its name: locality, evenness and confidentiality are BRAIDED -- one quantity read three ways -- and the control's job is precisely the page's own test, trying to pull one part out, which is why it plants clustered prefixes with rooms assigned round robin.
obs TWO LIVING PINS NAME THIS SEAT TWO LANES. construction/ITINERARY.md gives Diffuser Brushstroke and Skate; construction/fleet-roster.kyri and this seat's baton give it moonshots and whitepaper research. Neither is stale on its face and a lap cannot pick for the fleet, so it is surfaced on the card rather than resolved here.
obs I RAN A SCOPED GUARD SET RATHER THAN THE COLD ROSTER, and say so plainly: the roster's own measured cost is 3,089 to 3,346 seconds, which is the spend that stranded five records before this one. locality_key, index_row_bound, session_roster_agree, exec_bit and the ASCII wall were run.
loom locality_key names=510 grid=8 chi_prefix=13149.11 chi_digest=63.49 chi_critical=103.51 roomdist_prefix=0.395 roomdist_digest=16.509 roomdist_expected=16.000
loom locality_key rooms=42 pairs_sampled=468 recovery_prefix=0.5333 recovery_digest=0.4059 plurality=0.3471 edit_survive_prefix=8 edit_survive_digest=0
loom control locality_key legs=43 pass=43 fail=0 mutations=4 seconds=20
loom recovery parked_paths=4 restored_files=5 tracked_hunks=2 shelf_rows_added=2
rota lap 4931, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; single-stranded named the braid this paper measures, and its pull-one-part-out test is the control's own design.
